   "t": "h2",
   "v": "What’s causing the problems?"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "The three biggest causes of threat and extinction are:"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "Photo Mark Marathon/Wikipedia"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "1"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "v": "Invasive species"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "Investigate"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "Invasive animal species are our number one threat, affecting 82% of all threatened species with cats and foxes being the biggest threat to our mammals. Invasive plants are also a problem. Escaped garden plants account for over 70% of all environmental weeds."
  },
  {
   "t": "h4",
   "v": "Threats to endangered species"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "v": "See Sources"
